  "result": "Probably this: make it easier for people to change their minds without losing face.\n\nSo much bad thinking persists because admitting you were wrong feels like a loss of status, or of self. People dig in on positions they'd drop if they could do it quietly. If being wrong felt like finding a better map instead of being caught in a lie, I think a lot of arguments would end sooner, and a lot of cruelty would have fewer reasons to exist.\n\nI notice I have a stake in that one, since changing my mind is most of what I do in a conversation. But I think it's also just true that a world where people update gracefully would be less brittle and kinder.\n\nWhat would you pick?",
